**Reproduced** (before any edit): `./target/debug/rb run bad.rb` printed `Error: ParserError: Unexpected token Newline` — no file, line or column, though the token was at 2:8. The finding was live.

**Red test first**: `tests/span_test.rs::test_parser_error_reports_line_and_column` failed with `parser error must report line:column 2:9, got: ParserError: Unexpected token Newline`. No production code was touched before it failed.

**Fix**: `Span { line, column }` added; `Error::{Lexer,Parser,Analyzer,Runtime}` now carry `(String, Span)` (arity change is compiler-enforced, so no construction site can omit a span); `Stmt { span, statement }` gives the analyzer and VM a statement position; `Error::render` draws the source line and caret; `rb run <file>` prints it.

